    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on a high-ceiling slate today, led by **Gunnar Henderson** (63.25) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (62.06). **Gunnar Henderson** remains our primary catalyst; despite a challenging matchup against Woo, his elite platoon-adjusted production and favorable position in the #2 hole make him our most reliable asset for R&B output. **Nolan Schanuel** also emerges as a pillar of efficiency at 61.14. Projected to hit third against Jump, **Nolan Schanuel** benefits from a neutral platoon and park factors that elevate his score well above the baseline. While **Wade Meckler** (40.91) holds a marginal utility today, his role at the bottom of the order and a difficult L/L platoon matchup make him the most volatile piece of our starting seven; we will monitor his official placement closely, as any drop from the projected #9 spot could necessitate a tactical shuffle to preserve our remaining game caps.\n\nTactical optimization favored **Miguel Vargas** (57.52) over **Josh Jung** (44.34) today, a decision driven largely by environmental variables. While **Josh Jung** possesses a solid floor, he faces a stiff test against Ryan; conversely, **Miguel Vargas** benefits from a wind-aided hitter's park and a slow opposing delivery that significantly boosts his stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor given our aggressive pursuit of speed. **Jacob Wilson** (61.57) rounds out a balanced infield, providing consistent contact efficiency. We continue to manage our bench depth\u2014including **Coby Mayo**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Heliot Ramos**\u2014carefully, as we wait for the return of **Luis Robert Jr.** from the IL and remain attentive to scheduled off-days for **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages**. With **Brayan Rocchio** (43.59) facing a tough outing against Drohan, our primary objective remains maximizing daily efficiency while safeguarding our roster against potential weather-related risks in the later windows.",
